# Full GRIP Build — No Future Deferrals

**Mandate:** GRIP MUST be a 100% functioning app that creates and deploys full projects. We are building the full build now; there are no "future builds" to defer to.

## Do NOT

- Leave capabilities as "planned" or "later"
- Defer export, deploy, preview, full repo analysis, or chat-to-file persistence to a future phase
- Use mock data or placeholder API responses for these capabilities
- Implement only partial flows (e.g. export without real repo push, deploy without real Vercel URL)

## Do

- Implement, test, and verify: Export to GitHub, Deploy to Vercel, Preview (URL/StackBlitz), Full repo (tree + view/edit + analysis), Chat-to-files (save code to projectFiles), Project completion flow (Draft → Ready to export → Exported/Deployed)
- Reuse existing APIs and services (repository, fileStorageService, export route, deploy route); extend rather than duplicate
- Remove or replace mock data with real DB and real integrations for production readiness
- Verify each capability: export creates a real repo with content; deploy returns a real Vercel URL; preview loads URL or StackBlitz; Repo shows full tree; chat can save code to projectFiles

## Required capabilities (reference)

- **Export:** POST `/api/projects/[id]/export` — full project (repo files + projectFiles); user sees repo URL
- **Deploy:** POST `/api/projects/[id]/deploy` — deploy from project's GitHub repo; user sees live URL
- **Preview:** Project Preview tab — running app (URL iframe or Open in StackBlitz)
- **Full repo:** Repo tab — every folder and file (tree + view/edit); analysis for chat context
- **Chat-to-files:** Code generated in chat savable to projectFiles (create/update); appears in Generated files and export
- **Completion flow:** Status and CTAs: Run preview | Export to my GitHub | Deploy to Vercel

See `docs/FULL-BUILD-REQUIREMENTS.md` and `.cursorrules` → `full_grip_build`.
